{
  "title": "Prepositions and their cases",
  "note": "Each preposition takes a case, and some change meaning with the case: διά + genitive 'through', διά + accusative 'because of'. A final vowel drops before a vowel (δι’ αὐτοῦ, ἀπ’ ἀρχῆς), and π, τ become φ, θ before a rough breathing (ἀφ’ ἡμῶν, μεθ’ ἡμῶν). ἐκ becomes ἐξ before a vowel.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Perseus Digital Library (Smyth, Greek Grammar: prepositions)",
    "u": "https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/"
  },
  "items": [
    {
